WEBVTT

00:05:27.680 --> 00:05:30.300
and I'm not looking
at designing architecture like that.

00:05:30.324 --> 00:05:32.536
I'm just interested
in natural growth patterns

00:05:32.560 --> 00:05:36.736
and the beautiful forms
that only nature really creates.

00:05:36.760 --> 00:05:39.536
How that flows through me
and how that comes out

00:05:39.560 --> 00:05:41.176
is what I'm trying to understand.

00:05:41.200 --> 00:05:44.096
This is a scan through the human forearm.

00:05:44.120 --> 00:05:47.136
It's then blown up
through rapid prototyping

00:05:47.160 --> 00:05:48.736
to reveal its cellular structure.

00:05:48.760 --> 00:05:50.256
I have these in my office.

00:05:50.280 --> 00:05:53.296
My office is a mixture
of the Natural History Museum

00:05:53.320 --> 00:05:54.976
and a NASA space lab.

00:05:55.000 --> 00:05:57.816
It's a weird, kind of freaky place.

00:05:57.840 --> 00:05:59.936
This is one of my specimens.

00:05:59.960 --> 00:06:01.176
This is made --